===============
# OpenRange 0.0.3
===============

## Bug fixes
* Functions that rely on Internet resources (the OpenRange database and the
  OpenRange API) now fail gracefully, returning NULL along with an informative
  message rather than throwing an error, when the resource is unavailable,
  overloaded, or has changed, per CRAN policy and CRAN comments.
* The vignette now checks whether the OpenRange database is available and skips
  the chunks that require it when it is not, so that the vignette builds even
  when the resource cannot be reached.
* Tests that require an Internet resource are now skipped when that resource is
  unavailable.
* Records returned by the database or API that cannot be interpreted as spatial
  data now produce an informative message rather than an error.
* Functions no longer error when a query returns no records.


===============
# OpenRange 0.0.2
===============

## NEW FEATURES
* Updates to allow downloading multiple scenarios

## Bug fixes
* Declared a dependency on R (>= 4.1.0) in DESCRIPTION, per CRAN comments, since
  the package uses the native pipe (|>).


===============
# OpenRange 0.0.1
===============

## NEW FEATURES

* Initial development

## Bug fixes

* Replaced "T" with "TRUE" in OpenRange_load_species, per CRAN comments.
* Removed examples for non-exported function, per CRAN comments.
* Placed PostgreSQL in single quotes in the description, per CRAN comments.
* Added a web link to API documentation to the description, per CRAN comments.
* Removed default directories, per CRAN comments.
* Modified web link in description, per CRAN comment.